Documentations of your First Sprint : This sprint focused on the core logic of connecting a patient’s biological identity with their medical regimen.
●	Integrated Data Model: Developed a schema that links Biometric Logs (Pulse, Temp) and Prescription Schedules (Dosage, Frequency, Timing) to a single Patient ID.
●	Medication Logic Flow: Documented the backend logic for "Adherence Windows"—calculating when a medication is "Due," "Taken," or "Missed."
●	Vitals Threshold Mapping: Defined the "Safe Zones" for patient vitals; if data falls outside these ranges, the API is prepared to trigger an alert.
●	Initial Endpoint Mapping: Defined the structure for GET /patient/medications and POST /vitals/log.
Patch Notes and behaviors of your Current Sprint: 
v0.1.0 - The "Life-Link" Patch
1. Patient Vital Tracking (Live Data Behavior)
●	Added: Dynamic ingestion for heart rate and body temperature.
●	Behavior: The API now accepts high-frequency data packets. It validates that the data is numeric and within a human-possible range (e.g., rejecting a heart rate of 0 or 500) before saving.
2. Daily Medication Scheduler (Adherence Behavior)
●	Added: CRUD operations for patient medication lists.
●	Behavior: Users can now input a medication name and a "Daily Frequency." The system automatically calculates the next expected dose time based on the initial entry.
3. The "Missed Dose" Flagging System
●	Added: Initial logic for tracking adherence status.
●	Behavior: If a "Taken" confirmation is not received within a 2-hour window of the scheduled dose, the system updates the record status from Pending to Late.
4. Security & Privacy (Health Data Protection)
●	Added: Row-Level Security (RLS) in the database.
●	Behavior: Ensures that a Medical Provider can only view the vitals and medication history of patients specifically assigned to them, preventing unauthorized data leaks.


